. Prevailing wind is East F1, not F2. So no wind bonus), W7 kong (simple).  \nHand: B1 B2 B3 chow (all simples), pair F4 (North Wind = Seat Wind).  \nSo patterns:  \n- Seat Wind (F4 pair) = 2 pts  \n- All Simples (no honors except F4? Wait F4 is honor, so disqualifies All Simples) \u2192 so All Simples no.  \n- No Honors? Has F4, so no.  \n- Pung of Terminals or Honors? exposed T8, F2, W7: none are terminals/honors except F2 is honor? F2 is South Wind \u2192 yes, honor pung = 2 pts each? Actually \"Pung of Terminals or Honors\" = 1 pt per pung. So F2 pung = 1 pt.  \nAlso W7 kong counts as pung of simples, no extra. T8 pung same.  \n- Concealed Kong? No, W7 kong was exposed? Wait Gang W7 was from my history \"Gang W7\" \u2014 likely I added 4th W7 to an existing pung? Possibly concealed? My history: \"Peng T8, Play W1, Play T6, Play F3, Play B6, Peng F2, Play T9, Gang W7\" \u2014 did I have W7 pung concealed then gang? Possibly yes if I had 3 W7s and drew 4th. That could be concealed kong = 8 pts? No, \"Concealed Kong\" pattern worth 2 pts, not 8. Wait scoring list: Concealed Kong = 2 pts.  \n- Other: Chicken Hand? Not if I have \u22658 pts.  \n\nLet's tally if win with F4:  \nSeat Wind pair (2) + Pung of Honors (F2) (1) + Concealed Kong (W7) (2) = 5 pts so far. Possibly more: Last Tile? Not yet. Self Drawn? Not yet. All Pungs? No, I have chow B1B2B3.  \nSo 5 pts < 8, cannot win. Need more patterns.  \n\nIf win with B3:  \nThen pair = B3 (simple), so no seat wind. Patterns: F2 pung (1) + Concealed Kong (2) = 3 pts only.  \n\nSo actually neither reaches 8 pts yet with current hand, unless some patterns I missed: maybe \"Two Concealed Pungs\" \u2014 I have T8 exposed (Peng) so not concealed. F2 exposed. W7 kong maybe concealed? If W7 kong was from drawing 4th to concealed pung, then the pung was concealed, so that's 1 concealed pung? Actually \"Two Concealed Pungs\" = 2 pts, needs 2. I have only W7 possibly. Not enough.  \n\nGiven this, I'm far from winning; likely aim to reduce danger.  \n\n**Danger**:  \nUnshown tiles: F4=2, F1=2, B3=3, etc.  \nPrevious player's melds include T1, B7, T3T4T5 chow, W3W4W5 chow \u2014 they have many simples, may be close to win.  \nNext player meld T7 pung \u2014 also could be close.  \n\nDiscard safest: Which is least likely to give others pung/ chow?  \nB1: unshown B1=3, someone could need for chow (B1B2B3).  \nB2: unshown B4? Wait B2=4 left, B1B2B3 possible chow for others.  \nB3: unshown B3=3, possible pung for others.  \nF4: unshown F4=2, possible pung for others; also F4 is North wind = my seat wind, others may need for wind pung.  \n\nGiven seat wind is North, F4 is dangerous for others' seat wind? Prevailing wind is East (F1), so F4 not prevailing. Others' seat winds: mine is North, others unknown. But F4 likely less dangerous than B3? Possibly.  \n\nActually, other players' histories show many F4 plays: next player played F4 once, previous player played F2, not F4. F4 might be relatively safe.  \n\n**Temporary plan**: discard now to keep hand flexible.  \n\nChoose **Play B3** because it keeps B1B2B3 chow possibility and F4 pair possibility, and B3 is more dangerous (can complete others' B2B3B4 or B3B4B5 chows). Wait, but B1B2 also complete chow with discard B3? They'd need B2B3B4 or B1B2B3. Discarding B3 gives them B3 for pung possibly, but less likely than B2 for chow.  \n\nBetter: discard B1 keeps B2B3B3 \u2014 allows possible B3 pung draw and pair with F4. That\u2019s more flexible.  \n\nGiven scoring, I'm not winning soon; discard safer tile.  \n\nB1: chow danger for B1B2B3.  \nB2: chow danger for B1B2B3 or B2B3B4.  \nB3: pung/chow danger.  \nF4: wind pung danger.  \n\nLeast dangerous? Probably F4 because fewer players collect winds lately. Previous player played F2, not F4; next player played F4 once. Likely safe.  \n\nBut F4 is my seat wind, if I discard it, I lose chance for seat wind pair points. But I need 8 pts anyway, maybe discard F4 to keep all simples hand?  \n\nIf I discard F4, hand all simples: B1 B2 B3 B3 \u2192 possible B3 pair + B1B2B3 chow \u2192 winning wait on B3. Patterns: All Simples (2) + Concealed Kong (2) + maybe Two Concealed Pungs? I have only W7 possibly concealed. Not enough.  \n\nSo either way, not reaching 8.  \n\nChoose safest discard: **F4** because fewer people collect winds.  \n\nFinal decision:\n\nEvaluation: The hand is far from meeting the 8-point minimum to win, and the exposed melds do not provide enough scoring patterns. The priority is to discard safely to avoid giving other players what they need, while keeping some flexibility for future draws.\n\nReason: F4 (North Wind) is the seat wind, but given the current scoring outlook, it's unlikely to help reach 8 points. Among the options, F4 appears relatively safe based on game history showing limited wind collection by others. Discarding F4 maintains a hand of all simples, which could later combine with other patterns if fortunate draws occur.\n\nAnswer: Play F4"}
