ll Pungs if I make another pung instead of chow.\n\n- Unshown B3 count is 3, so drawing another B3 gives me a B3 pung (concealed), then I\u2019d need a pair for win. That could yield:  \n  All Pungs (6) + maybe Two Concealed Pungs (2) if the B3 pung and some other pung were concealed \u2014 but F2 and T8 melds are exposed, so only W7 kong is concealed? Actually W7 kong was Gang, was it concealed? In my history: \"Gang W7\" \u2014 that's adding fourth W7 to a concealed pung? Or exposed? Likely exposed if Gang after others saw it, but unclear. But still, Chi now would hurt.\n\nGiven all this, Chi B2 reduces scoring potential dramatically, while keeping hand closed (by passing) preserves chance for higher points through drawing into pungs. Also, with many B3 left, waiting for B3 to complete pung or pair is reasonable.\n\n---\n\n**Answer: Pass**"}
